-- title:
--   Residual transcendence of j(mathsf q^{qℓ}) along the Igusa branch
-- statement:
--   **Arithmetic data.** Let $q$ be a prime with $q\ge 5$, let $M'$ be a non-zero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ and $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; the hypothesis `hι` requires that some ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ send $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$.
--
--   **The function field.** Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$ (Laurent series over $L$) with $K=$ `laurentBaseChange L` of `xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M')`: that is, $K$ is the $L$-subfield of $L(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the field of $\mathsf q$-expansions of modular functions for $\Gamma_H(N_0)$, where $N_0=(q\ell)^2M'$ and $H=$ `levelH (q*ℓ) M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/N_0)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   **The base ring.** Let $A$ be a Henselian local discrete valuation domain with algebraically closed residue field, equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ its fraction field, with $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ and with $\xi$ in the image of $A\to L$, together with a compatible $A$-algebra structure on $K$. Let $j\in K$ be non-zero whose Laurent expansion is the image under `coeffEmb L` of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), the $\mathsf q$-expansion $\mathsf q^{-1}+\cdots$ of the modular invariant. Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$, and let $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$. Throughout, `chartAlgFin A K j` denotes the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, `jChartFin` denotes $j$ viewed in it, and `TwoChartIntegralModel A K j` is the scheme obtained by gluing the spectra of the $j$-finite and $j^{-1}$-finite chart algebras, with `toBase` its structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$.
--
--   **The supersingular point.** Let $y$ be a maximal ideal of `chartAlgFin A K j` containing the image of $\varpi$, and let `hss` require: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in `ssJSet q Ω`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no non-zero point killed by $q$.
--
--   **The rigidity hypothesis `hArig` (summarised here).** For every point $z$ of `TwoChartIntegralModel A K j` at which the germ of $\varpi$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, every point $y'$ of the affine chart $\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgFin A K j` mapping to $z$, and every verification that $j$ is supersingular at $y'$ in the sense above, `hArig` asserts the existence of a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma:A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[\![X_0,X_1]\!]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S:=W[\![X_0,X_1]\!]/\bigl(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v-fu\bigr)$, subject to seven clauses: (i) $e$ carries the germ of a constant $a\in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) the level automorphisms $\tau$ of $K$ attached (in the sense of `IsLevelAutAt`, with parameters $L$, $q\ell$, $\xi$, $q\ell$, $N_0$, $H$ and the matrix $\gamma^{-1}$) to $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserve the chart algebra; (iii) if moreover $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, such a $\tau$ acts trivially modulo $y'$; (iv) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and a $\tau$ acting trivially modulo $y'$, there are an automorphism $\theta$ of $S$ compatible with $e$ and the germ map, fixing the constants $C(w)$, a scalar $c\in W$ and a matrix $M$ over $W$ such that $\theta$ has linear part $M$ modulo the square of $(X_0,X_1)$, $c^{q+1}\equiv 1$, $M\equiv c\,\gamma$ entrywise modulo $\mathfrak m_W$, $c\equiv 1$ if $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, and $c\not\equiv 1$ if $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\ne\mathrm{id}$; (v) two primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$ containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$ but not both classes of $X_0,X_1$, and containing elements with linear parts $(a_1,b_1)$, $(a_2,b_2)\in\mathbb Z^2$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$, have distinct contractions to the stalk whenever $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$; (vi) for such a prime $P$ with linear part $(1,0)$, an element $a$ of the chart algebra has germ in the contraction of $P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$; (vii) `jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`, the series obtained from the $j$-expansion by substituting $\mathsf q^{q\ell}$ for $\mathsf q$, lies in $K$ and in the chart algebra, is congruent modulo $y'$ to a constant $a_0\in A$, and the germ of the difference corresponds under $e$ to a power series $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ with $e_0\ge1$ whose degree-$e_0$ form $\sum_{i\le e_0}h_{(i,e_0-i)}a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit for all $a,b\in W$ not both in $\mathfrak m_W$ with $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_W$.
--
--   **A chosen chart.** Fixed data $z,\varpi_z,y'$ as above are given, with `hϖz`, `hz`, `hy'` and `hss'` the corresponding conditions, and $y'$ is identified with $y$ by `hy'y`. Concretely given are $W_1$ (a complete discrete valuation domain), $\sigma_1$, $f_1,u_1,v_1$ with $u_1,v_1$ units, $f_1$ congruent to $X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$, and an isomorphism $e_1$ of the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ with $S=W_1[\![X_0,X_1]\!]/\bigl(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1-f_1u_1\bigr)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts the seven clauses (i)–(vii) above verbatim for this data.
--
--   **Blow-up data.** The ideal $J$ of the chart algebra is, by `hJ`, the infimum of the ideals $\tau^{-1}$ of the contraction, along the composite of the germ map with $e_1$, of the ideal generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$, taken over all $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$. The $A$-subalgebra $B$ of $K$ is, by `hB`, generated over the chart algebra by $\{x\in K:\exists\,i\in J,\ x\varpi_t=i\}$. A valuation subring $W$ of $K$ contains $B$ (`hBW`), and: `hR1` states that the chart algebra is contained in $B$ and that $K$ is the field of fractions of $B$; `hR2` states that $A\to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and that $B/(\varpi)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses) states that $W\cap L$ is the image of $A$, that $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that $y$ is the contraction of $\mathfrak m_W$ to the chart algebra, and that $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak m_W$; `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here) states that for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho$ from $B$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel the elements lying in $\mathfrak m_W$, compatible with $A\to\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ and equivariant for the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ via an element $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c)$ of [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) acting through `hAction`, with $c\ne1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\ne\mathrm{id}$; that those automorphisms preserve $B$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is reached from $\mathfrak m_W$ by such an automorphism with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$; that an element of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak m_W$ after all such automorphisms is divisible by $\varpi$; and that an automorphism preserving $y$ preserves $W$.
--
--   **The end.** Further, `hjK` and `hjC` place `jqNModC L (q*ℓ)` in $K$ and in the chart algebra; $m\ge1$ satisfies $\varpi^m=\varpi_t w$ with $w$ a unit. A finite set `ends` of subrings of $K$ is characterised by `hends`: a subring $O$ belongs to it exactly when there is a non-zero $a\in J$ such that, with $B_a$ the algebra generated over the chart algebra by $\{x: \exists i\in J,\ xa=i\}$, there is a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ with $O$ the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$, every element of $y$ a non-unit of $O$, and $B\not\subseteq O$. A member $O$ of `ends` is fixed, with $O\subseteq W$, $O$ local and Noetherian, the chart algebra contained in $O$, and $\varpi\in O$. Elements $c_x,c_y\in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, an isomorphism $\iota$ of the adic completion of $O$ with the crossing model $\widehat A[\![X_0,X_1]\!]/(X_0X_1-\varpi^m)$ and units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of the latter are given, subject to $c_xc_y=\varpi^m u$, to $\iota$ carrying constants from $A$ to constants (`hιc`), to $\iota(c_x)=\gamma_U\,U$ and $\iota(c_y)=\gamma_V\,V$, to $c_y$ lying in $\mathfrak m_W$ and to $c_x$ not lying in $\mathfrak m_W$.
--
--   **The Igusa valuation ring.** Finally, let $W_x$ be a valuation subring of $K$ such that: the chart algebra is contained in $W_x$ (`hB1`); $W_x\cap L$ is the image of $A$ (`hB2`); $\varpi\in W_x$ and $\mathfrak m_{W_x}=(\varpi)$ (`hB4`); every element of the chart algebra lying in $\mathfrak m_{W_x}$ lies in $y$ (`hB9`); and some element of $y$ does not lie in $\mathfrak m_{W_x}$ (`hB10`), so the centre of $W_x$ on the chart algebra is a prime strictly contained in $y$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Two assertions hold. First, there exists $t\in W_x$ such that for every polynomial $p\in A[X]$, if the value at $t$ of the image of $p$ in $L[X]$ lies in $W_x$ and in $\mathfrak m_{W_x}$, then every coefficient of $p$ lies in $\mathfrak m_A$. Second, the same holds with $t$ replaced by `jqNModC L (q*ℓ)` viewed in $K$ via `hjK`: for every $p\in A[X]$, if the value at it of the image of $p$ in $L[X]$ lies in $W_x$ and in $\mathfrak m_{W_x}$, then every coefficient of $p$ lies in $\mathfrak m_A$. Neither assertion restricts $p$ to be monic.
--
--   The statement expresses that the modular invariant $j(\mathsf q^{q\ell})$ is residually transcendental along a valuation of $K$ whose centre on the $j$-finite chart algebra is strictly smaller than the supersingular maximal ideal $y$ — the Igusa branch through the supersingular point, in the sense of the theory of Igusa curves and of the blow-up of the tame node. It is used in the construction of such an Igusa valuation subring at an end of the blown-up chart, cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_igusaValuationSubring_of_mem_ends_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_igusaValuationSubring_of_mem_ends_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked).
